We will build a simple **"Task Manager"** app where you can add tasks and view them.

### Prerequisites
*   Node.js installed (v14 or higher).
*   A code editor (VS Code recommended).

---

### Part 1: Project Structure
Create a folder named `my-app` and set up two subfolders: `client` (React) and `server` (Node).

```bash
mkdir my-app
cd my-app
mkdir client
mkdir server
```

---

### Part 2: The Backend (Node & Express)
This will handle the API to store data.

1.  **Initialize the server:**
    ```bash
    cd server
    npm init -y
    npm install express cors nodemon
    ```

2.  **Create `server/index.js`:**
    This file sets up the Express server and creates a dummy data array.

    ```javascript
    const express = require('express');
    const cors = require('cors');
    const app = express();
    const PORT = 5000;

    // Middleware
    app.use(cors()); // Allow React to talk to Node
    app.use(express.json());

    // Dummy Data (In a real app, this would be a Database)
    let tasks = [
        { id: 1, text: "Learn React", completed: true },
        { id: 2, text: "Build Node API", completed: false }
    ];

    // API Routes

    // 1. GET all tasks
    app.get('/api/tasks', (req, res) => {
        res.json(tasks);
    });

    // 2. POST new task
